# 4. Verify Network Interfaces

Run:

```bash
ip -br address
```

On the control plane you should see something similar to:

```text
lo      UNKNOWN   127.0.0.1/8
eth0    UP        10.0.2.15/24
eth1    UP        192.168.56.10/24
```

The important interface is:

```text
eth1
```

with:

```text
192.168.56.10
```

The other interface:

```text
10.0.2.15
```

is Vagrant's NAT interface.

This distinction is extremely important because both **kubelet and Flannel need to use the `192.168.56.x` network**.

