# 12. Configure the kubelet Node IP

This is one of the major fixes discovered while building the cluster.

Without explicitly setting the address, kubelet may register:

```text
10.0.2.x
```

instead of:

```text
192.168.56.x
```

Create the systemd directory on every node:

```bash
sudo mkdir -p /etc/systemd/system/kubelet.service.d
```

## Control Plane

On `controlplane`:

```bash
cat <<EOF | sudo tee \
/etc/systemd/system/kubelet.service.d/20-node-ip.conf
[Service]
Environment="KUBELET_EXTRA_ARGS=--node-ip=192.168.56.10"
EOF
```

## Node01

On `node01`:

```bash
cat <<EOF | sudo tee \
/etc/systemd/system/kubelet.service.d/20-node-ip.conf
[Service]
Environment="KUBELET_EXTRA_ARGS=--node-ip=192.168.56.11"
EOF
```

## Node02

On `node02`:

```bash
cat <<EOF | sudo tee \
/etc/systemd/system/kubelet.service.d/20-node-ip.conf
[Service]
Environment="KUBELET_EXTRA_ARGS=--node-ip=192.168.56.12"
EOF
```

On every machine:

```bash
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl restart kubelet
```

At this stage kubelet may repeatedly restart.

That is expected because Kubernetes has not been initialized yet.

