# 25. Create the Kubernetes User Private Key

On the control plane:

```bash
openssl genrsa \
  -out nginx-user.key \
  2048
```

Verify:

```bash
ls -l nginx-user.key
```

---

# 26. Generate the User CSR

Run:

```bash
openssl req \
  -new \
  -key nginx-user.key \
  -out nginx-user.csr \
  -subj "/CN=nginx-user/O=developers"
```

Verify:

```bash
openssl req \
  -in nginx-user.csr \
  -noout \
  -subject
```

Expected:

```text
CN = nginx-user, O = developers
```

---

# 27. Create `nginx-user-csr.yaml`

Now create the Kubernetes CSR manifest.

Run:

```bash
cat <<EOF > manifests/nginx-user-csr.yaml
apiVersion: certificates.k8s.io/v1
kind: CertificateSigningRequest
metadata:
  name: nginx-user
spec:
  request: $(cat nginx-user.csr | base64 | tr -d '\n')
  signerName: kubernetes.io/kube-apiserver-client
  expirationSeconds: 31536000
  usages:
    - client auth
EOF
```

Inspect it:

```bash
cat manifests/nginx-user-csr.yaml
```

Apply:

```bash
kubectl apply \
  -f manifests/nginx-user-csr.yaml
```

Check:

```bash
kubectl get csr
```

Initially:

```text
Pending
```

---

# 28. Approve the CSR

Approve:

```bash
kubectl certificate approve nginx-user
```

Verify:

```bash
kubectl get csr nginx-user
```

Expected:

```text
Approved,Issued
```

