# 32. Create the nginx-user kubeconfig

Create cluster configuration:

```bash
kubectl config set-cluster kubernetes \
  --server=https://192.168.56.10:6443 \
  --certificate-authority=/etc/kubernetes/pki/ca.crt \
  --embed-certs=true \
  --kubeconfig=nginx-user.conf
```

Add credentials:

```bash
kubectl config set-credentials nginx-user \
  --client-certificate=nginx-user.crt \
  --client-key=nginx-user.key \
  --embed-certs=true \
  --kubeconfig=nginx-user.conf
```

Create context:

```bash
kubectl config set-context nginx-user \
  --cluster=kubernetes \
  --user=nginx-user \
  --namespace=nginx-demo \
  --kubeconfig=nginx-user.conf
```

Activate context:

```bash
kubectl config use-context nginx-user \
  --kubeconfig=nginx-user.conf
```

Verify:

```bash
kubectl config view \
  --kubeconfig=nginx-user.conf
```

