# 62. Key Troubleshooting Fixes to Discuss

## Fix 1 — API Server Selected Wrong Interface

Initially Vagrant presented:

```text
10.0.2.15
```

as one of the control-plane interfaces.

We explicitly initialized Kubernetes with:

```bash
--apiserver-advertise-address=192.168.56.10
```

This ensures workers communicate with the API server over the Kubernetes private network.

---

## Fix 2 — kubelet Registered the Wrong IP

Because every VM has multiple interfaces, kubelet could register:

```text
10.0.2.x
```

We fixed this using:

```text
KUBELET_EXTRA_ARGS=--node-ip=192.168.56.x
```

for every machine.

---

## Fix 3 — Flannel Selected the Wrong Interface

The nodes contain:

```text
eth0 → 10.0.2.x
eth1 → 192.168.56.x
```

Flannel could select the NAT interface.

We modified its DaemonSet arguments to include:

```text
--iface=eth1
```

This forces Flannel traffic over:

```text
192.168.56.0/24
```

---

## Fix 4 — Flannel Requires the Correct Pod CIDR

Flannel expects:

```text
10.244.0.0/16
```

Therefore kubeadm was initialized with:

```bash
--pod-network-cidr=10.244.0.0/16
```

---

## Fix 5 — kubectl Could Not Connect

If kubectl reports:

```text
couldn't get current server API group list
```

or tries:

```text
http://localhost:8080
```

configure:

```bash
mkdir -p ~/.kube

sudo cp /etc/kubernetes/admin.conf \
  ~/.kube/config

sudo chown \
  $(id -u):$(id -g) \
  ~/.kube/config
```

---

## Fix 6 — Kubernetes CSR Pending

After creating the CSR:

```bash
kubectl get csr
```

may show:

```text
Pending
```

Approve it:

```bash
kubectl certificate approve nginx-user
```

It should become:

```text
Approved,Issued
```

---

## Fix 7 — Certificate Pending

cert-manager must be installed and operational before creating the Certificate resource.

Verify:

```bash
kubectl get pods \
  -n cert-manager
```

Then verify the issuer:

```bash
kubectl get clusterissuer
```

The issuer must show:

```text
READY=True
```

before relying on it.

---

## Fix 8 — Ingress Admission Webhook Errors

Before applying your Ingress, verify:

```bash
kubectl get pods \
  -n ingress-nginx
```

The Ingress controller/admission components must be operational.

Only then apply:

```bash
kubectl apply \
  --kubeconfig=nginx-user.conf \
  -f manifests/nginx-ingress.yaml
```

